# Normalise line endings in the repository, and check them out as LF everywhere.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true checks files out with
# CRLF, and Prettier — which defaults to endOfLine: "lf" — then fails
# `prettier --check .` on files nobody touched. Keep the working copy LF on all
# platforms so formatting is reproducible.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending normalised or diffed as text.
*.woff2 binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary